<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Regency of Spain and the Indies</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the Indies governed Spain in the name of the captive Ferdinand VII during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a>, replacing the Supreme Central Junta in 1810. Based at Cádiz, it summoned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> that wrote the constitution of 1812. Many juntas in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a>, including those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, refused to recognise it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-regency-of-spain-and-the-indies.jpg" alt="Council of Regency of Spain and the Indies" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagihuin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1812SpanishConstitutionMap.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
